264
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Di sala 2008'an da me dikan li vê derê vekir. Ev bi xwe eslê
me jî Cindirês e.
 
In 2008 we opened a shop here. We are originally from
Jindires.

265
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Aha asilê we jî Cindirês e, te di sala 2008'an de dikan li
vir vekiriye.
 
Aha, you are originally from Jindires, and you opened a shop
here in 2008.

266
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:40,000
Rast e keko, tu çi dikî?
 
That's right brother, what do you do?

267
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Wellehî em teraktorên... teraktor çêdikin. Erebeyên
teraktorê çêdikin.
 
By God, we... repair tractors. We fix tractor vehicles.

268
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Em ji kampa vir heya sînor em sererast dikin... Em xizmeta
vê miletî dikin kake.
 
We repair everything from the camp here to the border... We
serve this nation, brother.

269
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:56,000
Destê te sax be. Bi rastî em derbasî navçeya Şiyê bûn, me
pirs kir, ka em xêra xwe herin navçeyê...
 
God bless your hands. Honestly, we entered the Shiye
district, we asked around, saying let's go to the
district...

270
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Em hatin ketin sinaa te hesiya... Em ketin nav sînaê.
 
We came and entered your industrial area... We went into the
industrial area.

271
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Na navçeya Şiyê ye keko... Şiyê ye eva.
 
No, it's the Shiye district brother... This is Shiye.

272
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:08,000
Em bipirsin keko, çawa dibîne xebatê, sinayê çawa dibîne?
 
Let's ask, brother, how do you see the work, how do you see
the industry?

273
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:15,000
Şuxil çawa ye... tu ketî ser şuxilî. Me berê xebat dikir,
welleh elhemdulah şikir ji xwedê re, şuxil çêdibû.
 
How is the work... you got into the work. We used to work,
thank God, the work was getting done.

274
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Milletê me bar kirin, fîtelî hat, şuxlê me cûre yeke din bû,
yanê şuxilî kêm bû.
 
Our people moved away, trouble came, our work changed to
something else, meaning the work decreased.

275
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Weke berê şuxil qet nîne, em... ev miletê bar kirî, hate vê
derê... yanê weke min... ji aliyekî ve tu bibînî... em
dixwazin...
 
The work isn't like before, we... these people moved, came
here... meaning like me... if you look from one side... we
want...

276
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Em dixwazin miletê me yî ku reviyaye, ew jî werin.
 
We want our people who fled to come back.

277
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:39,000
Ez dibînim xwedanê teraktoran jî ketine gundên Şiyê û
navçeyê, gundê we û te di dît.
 
I see tractor owners have also come to the villages of Shiye
and the district, the villages you saw.

278
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Elhemdulelah şikir, tê dîtin dî.
 
Thank God, it is seen now.

279
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
Tu van teraktoran çawa dîbînî...
 
How do you see these tractors...

280
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:52,000
Ev teraktoran, wek cabaliyê ne, ew yê çepil in... Cebelê ne
navçeya Şiyê bûn berê... Ev teraktoran bi xwedê...
 
These tractors, they are like mountain ones, the ones with
arms... They were in the Shiye district mountains before...
By God, these tractors...

281
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Hûn wan sererast dikin... Cûreyên teraktoran çi ne?
 
You repair them... What are the types of tractors?

282
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:59,000
Hemî enwên teraktoran, em sererast dikin... Em wan dikin.
 
We repair all types of tractors... We do them.

283
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,000
Destê te sax be. Çend sal in te ev kar dikirî?
 
Bless your hands. For how many years have you been doing
this work?

284
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Welleh, kake em heştê yan 2008'an da me ev senedê dî dît...
 
By God, brother, we have been doing this since the 80s or
2008...

285
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:15,000
2008'an ez hatim navçeya Şiyê, weke em bixwe jî ji Cindirêsê
bûn. 2008'an ev der ji xwe re girt.
 
In 2008 I came to the Shiye district, originally we were
from Jindires. In 2008 I got this place.

286
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:17,000
Tu di vî karî de baş dît... te mesleheta vî karî qebûl kir?
 
Did you see good in this work... did you accept this
profession?

287
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:22,000
Ez ê dîrektoran meqbozlê dikim, te dî, ev pîşeyê min e.
 
I am fixing tractors, you see, this is my profession.

288
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
Tu pêşketina wê dibînî, wek...
 
Do you see its development, like...

289
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:32,000
Welleh pîşe, ez her kesî, vî karî xwe... razî me wek te
gotiye... min weha gotiye. Ev bi xwe ez jî... wek heye ez
razî me.
 
By God, the profession, everyone has their own work... I am
satisfied as you said... I said it like that. I am also...
as it is, I am satisfied.

290
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Destê we sax be kake.
 
Bless your hands brother.

291
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,000
Spas.
 
Thanks.

292
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Em derbas dibin, te gelek pirs, te got te tu qehr û
zehmetiyên wê qet nîne?
 
We are passing by, you have many questions, you said there's
no hardship or difficulties in it?

293
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Welleh, em ê derbas bibin, masîyê we ron bikin. Em weha we
dibînin tu serê xwe dît û ser çavên xwe dît, de xêr û
silamet be.
 
By God, we will pass by, let's light up your fish (make
things easier). We see you like this, you saw it with your
own eyes, may it be with goodness and safety.

294
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Xwedê jê razî be. Înşallah l'her demê hûn weha herin.
 
May God be pleased with him. God willing, you will always go
on like this.

295
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Înşellah...
 
God willing...

296
00:24:51,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Ehlen û sehlen, bixêr hatin.
 
Welcome, welcome.

297
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,000
Ev traktor bixwe, yê gundê Xelîl e.
 
This tractor belongs to the village of Xelil.

298
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Me wext da wê, emê du sê rojî de çêkin.
 
We gave it a time, we will fix it in two to three days.

299
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Em ê çêkin. Elhemdulelah, şikir ji xwedê re, me bi tebatî
temam kir.
 
We will fix it. Thank God, thanks to God, we finished it
patiently.

300
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:35,000
Û xwediyê traktorê jî ji gundê Xelîl e.
 
And the tractor owner is also from the village of Xelil.

301
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:40,000
Û mêrik hat cem me. Mêrik... yanî, mîna muazzezekî mukerrem
em ji wî re çêdikin.
 
And the man came to us. The man... I mean, we fix it for him
as an honored and respected person.

302
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Me çêkir. Şûnda mêrik heqê me da me û diçe qehweyek vedixwe
û mala xwe, diçe...
 
We fixed it. Afterwards the man pays us and goes to drink a
coffee and goes to his house...

303
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
Malê dinya de kîjan tişt tu... însan çibe weha...
 
Whatever happens in this world's wealth... whatever a person
is like...

304
00:25:49,000 --> 00:26:00,000
Yanî yê ku navê wî bi pere na... yanî ew pîşe, ev tişt, ev
miletî temam in... û xwediyê teraktora ev e. Jê gundê Xelîl
e...
 
Meaning the one whose name is not with money... meaning this
profession, this thing, this nation is complete... and this
tractor owner is this one. He's from the village of Xelil...

305
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:12,000
Û wexta me jê ra teraktor teslîm kir. Em tehsîlata xwe jê ra
werdigirin, welleh em gelek şikir e... em xelas bûn
ynşa'allah... û em teslîmatî didinê ev nebe qusur xwedê u
mala xwe, gundê xwe biçî.
 
And when we delivered the tractor to him. We received our
payment from him, by God we are very thankful... we are
finished God willing... and we give the delivery so there is
no flaw, for the sake of God, go to your house and village.

306
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:32,000
Ehlen û sehlen, ser serê me, ser çavên me. Her însan li dora
me kar dike ye.
 
Welcome, upon our heads, upon our eyes. Every person around
us works.

307
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

308
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Ehlen wa sehlen, kekê min.
 
Welcome, my brother.

309
00:26:51,000 --> 00:26:52,000
Tu çawa yî?
 
How are you?

310
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Maşallah, dinya germ e îro.
 
Wow, it's hot today.

311
00:26:54,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Erê welle, dinya germ e... ew tarîx e payîzê derbas e, me go
em dinya germ îro derkevin. Em te nas bikin.
 
Yes by God, the world is hot... the date of autumn has
passed, we said let's go out on a hot day today. Let's get
to know you.

312
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Bi xwedê navê min Dijwar e, ez ji gundê Erendê me.
 
By God, my name is Dijwar, I am from the village of Erende.

313
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:08,000
Û 2021'ê da me li Şiyê dikan vekiriye.
 
And in 2021 we opened a shop in Shiye.

314
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Ez trumpecî me.
 
I am a pump mechanic.

315
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:16,000
Te bi xwe, kake Dijwar, tu ji gundê Erendê yî, lê li navçeya
Şiyê te dikan vekiriye, dikanek trumpecî ye.
 
You yourself, brother Dijwar, you are from the village of
Erende, but you opened a shop in the Shiye district, it's a
pump mechanic's shop.

316
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,000
Erê. Trumpecî.
 
Yes. Pump mechanic.

317
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:23,000
2021'ê te li Şiyê dikan vekiriye... Em qala wî pîşeyê
bikin... tu çend sal in di vî dikanî de kar dikî?
 
In 2021 you opened a shop in Shiye... Let's talk about that
profession... how many years have you been working in this
shop?

318
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:26,000
Welle ji aliyê 15 sal e ez wî şixilê dikim.
 
By God, I've been doing this work for about 15 years.

319
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Kî derê te fêr kir... Tu fêrî vî pîşeyî bûyî?
 
Where did it teach you... Did you learn this profession?

320
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Li bajarê Helebê.
 
In the city of Aleppo.

321
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Bo wextê te ev şuxlî we dikir... tu di vî şuxlî de... wexta
kî tu di Helebê de bû çawa bû?
 
For the time you were doing this work... you in this work...
when you were in Aleppo, how was it?

322
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:39,000
Bixwedê şuxil hebûya... yanî ez bêm wextê berê em nînin weha
di... berî qeyranê weha.
 
By God there was work... meaning I should say we are not
like the old times... before the crisis like this.

323
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Bi fîtrê wî wextî yanî berê şixil pir baş bû, niha nîne...
 
With the nature of that time, I mean work was very good
before, now it's not...

324
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:49,000
Şuxil çawa ye? Kesê ku... dema kar hebe heye, lê hin dem qet
nîne!
 
How is the work? The person who... when there is work, there
is, but sometimes there is none at all!

325
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Yanî ew debara xwe mirov bike weke berê nîne, pir kêm bûye.
 
Meaning for a person to make a living, it's not like before,
it has decreased a lot.

326
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Û bi xwe jî hûn, dî wî tiştî de, tu perçeyan çawa peyda
dikî?
 
And you yourself, in that thing, how do you find parts?

327
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Bixwedê tiştên wisa hene em ji gundê din tînin, ji Cindirêsê
hene, ji Tirkiyê jî daxwaz dikin heger tişt.
 
By God there are such things we bring from the other
village, there are from Jindires, we also request from
Turkey if it's a thing.

328
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Ji perçeyên wê firotan heye?
 
Is there sales from its parts?

329
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Ew heye, pir ji mişteriyan dixwazin hin perçe bi firotin
tînin... li vî herêmî.
 
That exists, many customers want it, they bring some parts
by sale... in this region.

330
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Efrîn û vî alî me perê Tirkiye ye... Û ew alî dî de, dolar
e.
 
Afrin and our side is Turkish money... And on that other
side, it's dollars.

331
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Wextê tu parçeyek tînî da ku cîhê xwe çêkî, ferqa wê
buhabûneke çawa heye? Yanî perçeyên orjînal û yê din... ferq
heye?
 
When you bring a part to fix its place, what kind of price
difference is there? I mean original parts and the others...
is there a difference?

332
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:28,000
Bixwedê qat bi qat çûye ser... Yanî heger wextê perçeyek
pênc dolar be... niha bûye bîst dolar, yanî...
 
By God it has multiplied... I mean if at the time a part was
five dollars... now it has become twenty dollars, meaning...

333
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Gelek perçe hene bi dolar difiroşin... bi hezaran jî heye.
Ev ferq heye.
 
There are many parts they sell for dollars... there are even
in thousands. This difference exists.

334
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:42,000
Û hûn, di van her duyan de, vî navçeyê de di nav gundê xwe
de... çima ne Erendê û çima Şiyê?
 
And you, in both of these, in this district in your
village... why not Erende and why Shiye?

335
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Vî gundî me dikan vekiriye, ji ber heval û mişteriyan. Em jî
ev heval, hatin me li Şiyê vekir, piranî hatin vir.
 
We opened the shop in this village, because of friends and
customers. We also, these friends, came and we opened in
Shiye, mostly they came here.

336
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Ev ji derveyê Şiyê ne, hemî navçeyan ketine sînaê, ma
hewceyî sînaê heye li vir?
 
These are from outside Shiye, all districts have entered the
industrial area, is there a need for an industrial area
here?

337
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Sînaeyek çêbûye li vira... sînaeyek çêkirine.
 
An industrial area has been built here... they built an
industrial area.

338
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:03,000
Sînaê girtine... ji bo me em dikarin xebata xwe bikin weke
berê... em baş in weha...
 
They secured the industrial area... for us we can do our
work like before... we are fine like this...

339
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Em spasiya we dikin kake.
 
We thank you brother.

340
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Xwedê ji we razî be... Em spasiya we jî dikin... me dîtin we
hatin, em spas dikin.
 
May God bless you... We also thank you... we saw you came,
we say thank you.

341
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Her serkeftî bin... û bixêr hatin we we.
 
Always be successful... and welcome to you all.

342
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Xwedê hefaz kirî. Bi tawfîq. Serkeftî bin.
 
May God protect. With success. Be successful.

343
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:37,000
Xwedê te razî be. Gelek spas.
 
May God bless you. Thank you very much.

344
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Dembaş, kake.
 
Good day, brother.

345
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Dembaş, ehlen û sehlen... Ser çava.
 
Good day, welcome... You're welcome.

346
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:58,000
Xwedê te razî be. Em derbasî navçeya te bûn. Ciyê navçeyê di
me de sê çar cîh e, dikan e... hûn çendin e?
 
May God bless you. We entered your district. The district
place for us is three four places, shops... how many are
you?

347
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Em sê çar dikan in li navçeya Şiyê, û min dikan li Cindirêsê
jî heye...
 
We are three four shops in the district of Shiye, and I have
a shop in Jindires too...

348
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:07,000
Bi rastî ji yekem derbasî cem we bûm min dît, te ji min re
xeberek da got dê û bav û bapîrên te pêncî sal in, ev kar û
senhetî tê de dikin.
 
Actually, when I first came to you, I saw you gave me some
information, saying that your parents and grandparents have
been doing this work and trade for 50 years.

349
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Baş e, te xwest nexwest, em derbasî gundekî bibin, em sirrê
zeytê ji we nas bikin, çarek çarek sirra xwe jî, wextê em
derbasî cem we bûn.
 
Well, whether you wanted it or not, when we go to a village,
we learn the secret of olive oil from you, sometimes your
secrets too, when we came to you.

350
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Bi Xwedê, navê şîrketa me, şîrketa Şêxo ye.
 
By God, the name of our company is Şêxo Company.

351
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Xalê min Ebo Arif e.
 
My uncle is Ebo Arif.

352
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Ortamê me Ebo Lawend e. Xalê min Ewcî.
 
Our partner is Ebo Lawend. My uncle Ewcî.

353
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Em zeytê didin, vî mecalî de dişuxilin.
 
We sell olive oil, we work in this field.

354
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:27,000
Bi Xwedê, zeyt tesdîr hebe, pir baş e.
 
By God, if olive oil is exported, it is very good.

355
00:30:27,000 --> 00:30:34,000
Lê naha ka, sûkên zeytê ji bo bazirganan? Çawa ye, çawa ye
sûkê zeytê yên Helebê û yên bajarê din?
 
But now, how is the olive oil market for the merchants? How
is it, how is the olive oil market in Aleppo and other
cities?

356
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Bi Xwedê, hedîdê zeytê me gelek e, heştê nodî de weha
şixulandin, xêr e, ji bo ku tesdîr tineye.
 
By God, our limit of olive oil is a lot, we worked like this
in the eighties and nineties, it's good, because there is no
export.

357
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:43,000
Vêca em tiştekî, milet dîşe.
 
So it's something, the people go with it.

358
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Çawa? Gelo aliyê cotkaran da tu dibînî, mizarî'an de, te çi
dibînî?
 
How? As for the farmers, as you see, regarding the
agricultural workers, what do you see?

359
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:56,000
Bi Xwedê muzarî' xweş xizmet dike, avdan dike, mesrefê lê
dike, bes weye, ku, sûkê zeytê si'ir tine.
 
By God, the farmer serves well, waters it, spends on it, but
the thing is, there is no price in the olive oil market.

360
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Si'ir tine. Sernavê vê tiştî jî êşekî wê hene, kêm?
 
There is no price. On top of this, they also have some pain,
right?

361
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:00,000
Êşekî muzarî' e, heye.
 
The farmer does have pain, yes.

362
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,000
Êşekî heye.
 
He has some pain.

363
00:31:01,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

364
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,000
Gerek si'ir ji vî zêdetir ba.
 
The price should have been higher than this.

365
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Lema mesref giran e.
 
Because expenses are heavy.

366
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Her tenekê zeyt, avdan dibe, çawa dibe, vedan dibe, cût
dibe, gişt jî biha ye. Mûne jî biha ye. Tiştek din jî biha
ye, made zeytê me.
 
Every tin of olive oil, requires watering, how it's managed,
picking, plowing, it's all expensive. Provisions are also
expensive. Everything else is expensive, except our olive
oil.

367
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Te... naha em bîn ta, got 5-6 sal in, hûn bi vî karî de
dikin. Wexta kar e rast e.
 
You... now as we were saying, you said you have been doing
this work for 5-6 years. The time for work is real.

368
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:28,000
Erê, welleh erê, rast e, ev kar e, rast e.
 
Yes, by God, yes, it's true, this is the work, it's true.

369
00:31:28,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Zeyt naha, te dibînî lê ber biha ve qasî wê dibe?
 
Olive oil now, do you see its price going up that much?

370
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Bi Xwedê naha di haliyan bihabûn tine. Sûk cemidî ye, ber vê
jî em hîvî ne, sûk biqelibe bibe baş.
 
By God, right now there is no price increase. The market is
frozen, because of this we hope the market will turn around
and become good.

371
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Erê welleh rast e.
 
Yes, by God, it's true.

372
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,000
Eceba ev mewsim, zeyt biha nabe? Li çî?
 
I wonder if this season, olive oil won't get expensive? For
what reason?

373
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Bi Xwedê, gerek de'mek hebe pê.
 
By God, there needs to be some support for it.

374
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Lema... bi Xwedê hîn wisa be, muzarî' wê gişt ji birçîna
bimrin.
 
Because... by God if it stays like this, the farmers will
all die of hunger.

375
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Bêguman wê wisa be. Naha ez dibînim, pir kesan hene ku
pereyan girê nadin, wê zeytê xwe halî didin.
 
Doubtlessly it will be like that. Now I see many people who
don't care about the money, they keep their olive oil.

376
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:54,000
Erê, ev kes naha, haliyan, bi vî zeytê îhtîfaz dikin, lê
nafroşin.
 
Yes, these people now, currently, are holding onto this
olive oil, they aren't selling it.

377
00:31:54,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Îhtîfaz dikin, heta si'ir biha dibe. Mesele, hinek mizarî',
milet heye mesele, gişt, sedî nefirot.
 
They are holding onto it until the price goes up. For
example, some farmers, some people for example, didn't sell
a hundred percent.

378
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Vêca şert dibe me lê, sedî, zirarê lê nakim.
 
So it becomes a condition for us, I don't cause a hundred
percent loss.

379
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Û ev tişt naha jî hene.
 
And these things still exist now.

380
00:32:06,000 --> 00:32:11,000
Her kes jî we nesîbê xwe. Xezal e, ji bazûtir tine. Kes
riziqê kesî naxwe.
 
Everyone gets their share. It's like a gazelle, nothing is
faster. No one eats someone else's provision.

381
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Erê, erê.
 
Yes, yes.

382
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:22,000
Em spasîya we dikin, û spasîya şîrketa we jî dikin. Bi rastî
amade ne, belkî vîdyoya me temam be, temam nebe, em ê dîsa
jî herin înşelleh.
 
We thank you, and we thank your company too. Truly we are
ready, maybe our video will be finished, maybe not, we will
go again God willing.

383
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Ser çava, û ser çava. Û em bi xwe jî, şahneyê jî dişuxilin.
Şîrketa xêrat Heleb, Henan.
 
Upon my eyes, upon my eyes (You are welcome). And we
ourselves also work in shipping. The company of charities in
Aleppo, Henan.

384
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Xwediyê şîrketê jî em in... Rebet e, Reşîd e, Hemûd e, gundê
Hisên e.
 
We are the owners of the company too... Rebet, Reşîd, Hemûd,
from the village of Hisên.

385
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:37,000
Ew şebabên wê jî, pir xort in, pir rind in. Û kefale 100 ji
100î em didin.
 
The young men there are also very strong, very good. And we
give a 100 out of 100 guarantee.

386
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Em spasîya we dikin, û we bi xweşbînî dibînin.
 
We thank you, and we look at you with optimism.

387
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Ser çavê me, ehlen û sehlen. Ser çavî, mamo.
 
You are welcome, upon our eyes. Upon my eyes, uncle.

388
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:46,000
